1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:09,470
Swarm detail two. Read the cockpit. Five agents talking at once is noise, unless you can see who's doing what.

2
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:22,732
So every agent gets a face on the live card. A double ring is the lead, a dashed plus an open seat. A bright ring is on a turn, an amber dot has messages waiting, and a faded face is idle.

3
00:00:23,232 --> 00:00:28,572
This is a Crew: a lead, up to four workers, and a ten dollar ceiling.

4
00:00:29,932 --> 00:00:39,080
The question is whether a five person team should split billing out of its Rails monolith. The lead takes the first turn, then fills its four seats.

5
00:00:40,532 --> 00:00:52,080
Security and the cost skeptic wear amber dots: the lead addressed them, so their turns are queued. When the lead's turn ends, its face fades. Idle costs nothing.

6
00:00:53,632 --> 00:01:00,348
Then a worker's answer names the lead. An amber dot lands, and the lead lights up for its next turn.

7
00:01:01,332 --> 00:01:10,208
Beside the faces, four meters run toward the plan's ceilings: turns, time, fresh tokens, and cost, with the burn rate per minute.

8
00:01:11,332 --> 00:01:19,488
The Map tab draws who addressed whom. The lead fans out to every worker, and the crossings are workers challenging each other.

9
00:01:21,832 --> 00:01:30,436
A minute and a half in, the lead concludes. The outcome stays on top: keep billing in the monolith, and draw the boundary inside Rails.

10
00:01:31,232 --> 00:01:36,014
Spend splits the sixty four cents by agent. Produced holds the report.

11
00:01:36,932 --> 00:01:46,848
Activity is every turn and how long it took. About keeps the task and the transcript. And Agents gives each one's role, turns and cost.

12
00:01:48,032 --> 00:01:55,596
The channel is the record. The cockpit is what you check at a glance: who's working, who's waiting, and what it's costing.

13
00:01:56,196 --> 00:01:58,802
Next, how big a crew a question needs.

14
00:02:01,502 --> 00:02:05,484
Keelson. Lay the keel, raise the ribs.

